 "notes": "TASEH CD102 haloscope run, 4.70750-4.79815 GHz (19.4687-19.8436 ueV). 95% C.L. observed upper limit on |g_agamma| extracted pixel-wise from the red curve in Fig. 2 (raster PNG in the e-print), axis-calibrated to the labelled ticks, then block-median downsampled to ~100 points. Paper assumes rho_a = 0.45 GeV/cm^3 (canonical value, no rescaling) and 100% axion DM. Quoted limits range 5.3e-14 to 8.9e-14 GeV^-1 with average 8.2e-14; extracted curve averages 8.19e-14. Narrow dips (rescanned bins reaching 5.3e-14) are smoothed by the column-median + downsampling, so the curve mostly tracks the ~8e-14 envelope. Two RFI-excluded frequency ranges (4.71017-4.71019 and 4.74730-4.74738 GHz, no limits placed) and boundary-bin spikes were removed before downsampling.",
